Subject: [PATCH] JSFX: start the renderer when the editor is displayed

A host that draws the plug-in's frames itself -- uapmd-cmp, through the
framebuffer UI C entry points -- never calls showUI(): there is no view for it to
create. showUI() was the only thing that started the thread running @gfx, so the
editor stayed blank for ever while every other part of the extension answered
normally.

Being displayed is what makes it draw, which is what the extension already
claimed. start() is idempotent, so the showUI() path is unchanged, and hiding
still leaves it ticking slowly so that it notices being shown again.

Upstream: applied to uapmd's own tree; delete this patch once the submodule
carries it.

diff --git a/source/uapmd-format-jsfx/src/JsfxFramebufferUI.cpp b/source/uapmd-format-jsfx/src/JsfxFramebufferUI.cpp
index d66833b1..6b91cad6 100644
--- a/source/uapmd-format-jsfx/src/JsfxFramebufferUI.cpp
+++ b/source/uapmd-format-jsfx/src/JsfxFramebufferUI.cpp
@@ -236,8 +236,19 @@ namespace uapmd_jsfx {
     }
 
     void JsfxFramebufferUI::displayed(bool value) {
-        std::lock_guard lock{state_mutex_};
-        displayed_ = value;
+        {
+            std::lock_guard lock{state_mutex_};
+            displayed_ = value;
+        }
+        // Being displayed is what makes the renderer run. A host that draws the frames
+        // itself never goes near showUI() -- there is no view for it to create -- so if
+        // this did not start the renderer, nothing would, and the editor would stay
+        // blank for ever. start() is idempotent, so the showUI() path is unaffected.
+        //
+        // Not stopped on the way out: a hidden editor keeps ticking slowly so that it
+        // notices being shown again, which is what desiredFrameRate() is about.
+        if (value)
+            start();
     }
 
     uint32_t JsfxFramebufferUI::desiredFrameRate() {
